{"source_passage_id": "HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING-P0005-PASSAGE", "text": "How to perform MMT\n• Patients are asked to hold a position against a therapist’s resistance.\n• It is important to stabilize proximal part of the area being tested to reduce compensatory action by muscles other than those being tested\n• Resistance needs to be applied gradually (\"meet my resistance\" or \"don't let me move you\") in the opposite direction of muscle being tested\n• Both sides should be tested to provide a comparison", "document_id": "HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING", "document_title": "Lecture 7.1 - Manual Muscle Testing", "source_file": "21 - 7.1 Manual Muscle Testing 手動肌肉測試.pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING-P0005"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING-P0005", "document_id": "HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING", "document_title": "Lecture 7.1 - Manual Muscle Testing", "source_file": "21 - 7.1 Manual Muscle Testing 手動肌肉測試.pdf", "page_number": 5, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 5, "pdf_page": 5, "formatted": "21 - 7.1 Manual Muscle Testing 手動肌肉測試.pdf, slide 5 (PDF p. 5)"}], "slide_number": 5, "section_ids": ["HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING-P0005", "HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING-PART02", "HHS4867-L07-MANUAL-MUSCLE-TESTING", "HHS4867-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS4867 - Functional Movement Science", "Lecture 7.1 - Manual Muscle Testing", "MMT procedure and testing positions", "How to perform MMT"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
